From: rlw@ida.org (Richard Wexelblat)

Re Fort Ludious

The problem is that you have confused the Castle (appearing below the
Medusa level in every game) with Fort Ludios (that appears in most, but
not all, games).

Fort Ludios, if there is one in your game, will be accessable from a
magic portal in a treasure room somewhere between levels 10 and 20.  To
get across the moat you'll need water breathing or levitation.  The
entry door (on the far right) is a normal portal can can be opened with
knock, a wand of striking, kicking (sometimes), etc.  As a matter of
fact, hang around long enough and sometimes a monster will even open it
for you.

You will find $* treasure galore in the Fort.  Magic and implements
only as normal monsters drop them.  Lots of wands from the soldiers,
though.

My rule of thumb is: if I have found a friendly priest to give gold to
or need the experience for the quest then I'll take out Ludios.
Otherwise I'll ignore it.  If at all possible, have sleep protection
before wading in as one of the soldiers is sure to have a sleep wand.
(Though this is less important in 3.1.3)

